To share the "catch-all" IP route only with specific BGP neighbors, configure an export policy to selectively advertise the default route (0.0.0.0/0) to designated peers. Here's the required CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router policy-options
begin
prefix-list "DEFAULT_ROUTE"
    prefix 0.0.0.0/0 exact
exit
policy-statement "EXPORT_DEFAULT"
    entry 10
        from
            prefix-list "DEFAULT_ROUTE"
        exit
        action accept
        exit
    exit
commit
exit

configure router bgp
group "TARGET_GROUP"
    neighbor 192.0.2.1
        family ipv4
        export "EXPORT_DEFAULT"
    exit
    neighbor 192.0.2.2
        family ipv4
        export "EXPORT_DEFAULT"
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
1. Create a `prefix-list` matching the default route (0.0.0.0/0).  
2. Define a route policy (`EXPORT_DEFAULT`) that permits advertisement of this route.  
3. Apply the policy as an `export` directive under each target neighbor in their respective BGP group.  

Replace `TARGET_GROUP` with your group name and `192.0.2.1/192.0.2.2` with the actual neighbor IPs. Peers without this policy will not receive the default route.
