To configure your Nokia 7750 SR to advertise the default route (0.0.0.0/0) only to specific BGP neighbors, use the following CLI commands. This involves creating a route policy to match the default route and applying it as an export policy to the targeted neighbors:

```cli
# Create a prefix list to match the default route
/configure router policy-options prefix-list "DEFAULT_ROUTE"
prefix 0.0.0.0/0 exact
exit

# Create a route policy to advertise the default route
/configure router policy-options policy-statement "EXPORT_DEFAULT"
entry 10
from prefix-list "DEFAULT_ROUTE"
action accept
exit
commit

# Apply the policy to specific BGP neighbors
/configure router bgp
group "TARGET_GROUP"  # Replace with your group name or use existing group
neighbor <neighbor_IP>
export "EXPORT_DEFAULT"
exit
exit
```

### Explanation:
1. **`prefix-list "DEFAULT_ROUTE"`**: Defines the default route (0.0.0.0/0) for matching.
2. **`policy-statement "EXPORT_DEFAULT"`**: Advertises the default route when applied.
3. **`export "EXPORT_DEFAULT"`**: Applied directly to the neighbor(s) (under their group or individual configuration) to limit the advertisement to only those peers.

Replace `TARGET_GROUP` with the BGP group containing your specific neighbors, and `<neighbor_IP>` with the actual neighbor IP addresses. Neighbors not targeted by this export policy will not receive the default route.
