To configure BGP on your Nokia 7750 SR to resolve next-hops for labeled IPv4 routes using tunnels instead of the default method, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4
                        resolution any
                    exit
                    family vpn-ipv4
                        resolution any
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

If you need to modify the BGP next-hop when advertising routes to specific neighbors, also apply `next-hop-self` under the relevant BGP group or neighbor configuration:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            next-hop-self
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This setup:
1. Enables VPN route reflector forwarding (`enable-rr-vpn-forwarding`) to handle next-hop resolution in a dummy VRF
2. Configures tunnel-based next-hop resolution for both labeled IPv4 unicast and VPN-IPv4 routes
3. Allows resolution using any available tunnel type (adjust `resolution any` to `resolution filter` with specific tunnels if needed)
4. Optional: Forces next-hop modification via `next-hop-self` when readvertising routes

The tunnel resolution applies to all IPv4 labeled routes, including VPN-IPv4 and labeled unicast, using MPLS transport tunnels for next-hop reachability.
