To configure BGP to hide your real AS numbers when advertising routes to a peer, use the following commands. Replace `<virtual_as>` with a chosen private AS number (e.g., 64512) and `<neighbor_ip>` with the peer's IP address:

```console
configure router bgp
    group "EXAMPLE_GROUP"
        neighbor <neighbor_ip>
            local-as <virtual_as> no-prepend-global-as
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Key details**:
- `local-as <virtual_as>` replaces your true ASN (`65535`) in the session with a virtual AS.
- `no-prepend-global-as` ensures your real ASN (`65535`) is **never added** to the AS_PATH in routes sent to the peer.
- The peer will only see `<virtual_as>` in the AS_PATH, hiding both your true local AS and backbone AS.

> **Note**: This doesn't modify existing AS_PATH entries from internal routes. Use route policies if backbone AS stripping is required.
