To automatically tag outgoing BGP routes with a metric of 15000 when the original route lacks it, configure the `link-bandwidth` settings under the relevant BGP group or neighbor. Use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> link-bandwidth
    default-bandwidth 15000
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This ensures routes without an existing metric inherit 15000 when advertised to peers. For neighbor-specific application:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> link-bandwidth
    default-bandwidth 15000
exit
```

Replace `<neighbor-ip>` with the neighbor's IP address. This configuration preserves existing metrics and applies only when the original route has no metric.
