To achieve automatic session termination when a peer's IP isn't allowed by the `core-routes` filter, configure BGP dynamic neighbors with the specific prefixes permitted by the filter:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "dynamic-core"
        dynamic-neighbor
            prefix <core-routes-prefix-1/prefix-length>
            prefix <core-routes-prefix-2/prefix-length>
            ...
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key Details**:  
- Replace `<core-routes-prefix-1/prefix-length>`, `<core-routes-prefix-2/prefix-length>` etc. with the **exact IP prefixes** permitted in your `core-routes` filter.  
- Sessions from peers outside these prefixes will automatically fail to establish.  
- Existing sessions will drop immediately if their source IP no longer matches any configured prefixes after configuration changes.  

**Example**: If `core-routes` permits `10.0.0.0/8` and `192.168.0.0/16`:  
```cli
configure router bgp
    group "dynamic-core"
        dynamic-neighbor
            prefix 10.0.0.0/8
            prefix 192.168.0.0/16
        exit
    exit
exit
```
