To enforce a 5-minute (300-second) countdown for all route types during extended network issues, overriding the peer's advertised LLGR timers, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group "<group-name>"
            neighbor <ip-address>
                graceful-restart
                    long-lived
                        helper-override-restart-time 0
                        helper-override-stale-time 300
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key Details:**  
- `helper-override-restart-time 0` immediately triggers the LLGR phase upon session failure (bypassing peer restart timers).  
- `helper-override-stale-time 300` forces a 300-second (5-minute) LLGR retention window for all AFI/SAFI advertised by the peer.  
- Replace `<group-name>` and `<ip-address>` with your BGP group and neighbor IP.  

This configuration ensures routes from the peer are preserved for exactly 5 minutes during outages, regardless of the peer's advertised timers.
