To stabilize BGP sessions with cranky peers during maintenance reboots and allow routes to linger longer, configure BGP Graceful Restart with an extended stale routes timer:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 900
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**  
- `graceful-restart` enables the router to preserve peer routes during their restart  
- `stale-routes-time 900` keeps routes in the RIB for 900 seconds (15 minutes) after session reset  
- This prevents immediate route flapping and gives legacy peers ample time to stabilize  

For neighbors requiring specific settings, apply the configuration at the group or neighbor level instead of globally. The timer value (900) can be adjusted between 1-3600 seconds based on your maintenance window needs.
